					]
				},
				{
					"id": "t-tnmnO6XoBSJqVlT",
					"name": "Enhanced Dodge",
					"reference": "B52",
					"local_notes": "Lore: A further step up from an ordinary Aspect Warrior's already-formidable evasion, after centuries of nothing else.\n\nDesign: A further Enhanced Dodge 1 (B52, 15 points), stacking with Aspect Training's own level for Enhanced Dodge 2 total.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"points_per_level": 15,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 1
				},
				{
					"id": "tQpbPrAUBSwi4n4m9",
					"name": "Combat Reflexes",
					"reference": "B43",
					"local_notes": "Lore: An Exarch has refought the same battle-role for centuries and simply does not freeze.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Combat Reflexes (B43), 15 points, the same trait this project's Astartes and Ork Warboss packages use for veteran-tier battlefield composure.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"base_points": 15
				},
				{
					"id": "teYzuPF6EevVcSP0I",
					"name": "Trained By A Master",
					"reference": "B90",
					"local_notes": "Lore: An Exarch's chosen weapon-form (the shrine's own signature blade, fusion gun, or reaper launcher) is drilled to a level no ordinary Aspect Warrior reaches, matching the fiction's treatment of an Exarch as an unmatched duelist within their Aspect's own art.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Trained By A Master (B90), 30 points, one weapon-art.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"base_points": 30
				},
				{
					"id": "trtS5GyeZ2xkClL_f",
					"name": "Weapon Master (Aspect Weapon)",
					"reference": "B99",
					"local_notes": "Lore: See Trained By A Master, above; the two together are how GURPS models a genuine master duelist.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Weapon Master, one weapon (B99), 20 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"base_points": 20
				},
				{
					"id": "tdTCz7MMkB5AQrnik",
					"name": "Enhanced Parry",
					"reference": "B52",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Centuries of the same duel, refought against every kind of foe, until the block is reflexive.\n\nDesign: Enhanced Parry 2, one weapon (B52, 5/level, 10 points).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 2
				},
				{
					"id": "twq3txcHTzryYtbP0",
					"name": "Lost to the Path (Warrior)",
					"reference": "B151",
					"local_notes": "As Fanaticism (single-minded devotion to the Path itself, here the Path of the Warrior): an Exarch cannot set the mantle down and walk away as an ordinary Aspect Warrior does when their years in the shrine end. See the top-level \"Lost to the Path\" entry above for the full design note; duplicated here as its own child so this container's point total is self-contained.\n\nLore: See the top-level \"Lost to the Path\" entry above.\n\nDesign: Fanaticism (B151, -15 points), redirected onto the Path itself; see the top-level entry above.",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"base_points": -15
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "T_fVswK6ShWHUFBRF",
			"name": "Aspect: Dire Avenger",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The most numerous Aspect and every shrine-world's backbone: disciplined shuriken-catapult skirmishers who hold a line and cover a retreat as readily as they lead an assault.\n\nDesign: Net 3 points, per-Aspect flavour lens, matching the Ork Klan lens pattern.",
			"tags": [
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari"
			],
			"children": [
